  "cards": [
    {"id": "A01", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Deep torn wound at the back of the head. Not a fall.",
     "prop": {"death.cause": "blow", "wound.shape": "torn"}},
    {"id": "A02", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Wristwatch, water inside, stopped at 23:41."},
    {"id": "A03", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Notebook: \"Holt - crates short again. Report Monday.\"", "motive_of": "P_Holt",
     "prop": {"cargo.count": "short"}},
    {"id": "A04", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Notebook: \"Owe N.V. $40 - pay Friday.\"", "motive_of": "P_Nora",
     "prop": {"morrow.debt": "owed"}},
    {"id": "A05", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Notebook: \"AGATHA - manifest wrong. Cleared by [smudged]. Meet H.M. 23:30, P5.\"",
     "at": [["P_Morrow", "Pier5Edge", "23:30", "23:41"]]},
    {"id": "A06", "kind": "anchor", "object": true, "text": "Boathook wedged in the pilings under the pier. Ash shaft, brass hook, tar on the grip."},
    {"id": "A07", "kind": "anchor", "object": true, "text": "Broken whisky bottle, Lighthouse label, near the edge."},
    {"id": "A08", "kind": "anchor", "object": true, "text": "Docker's bale hook on the fish crates, wet. The crane gang's."},
    {"id": "A09", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Edge lamp: bulb unscrewed, not burnt out. Eight feet up, nothing to stand on.",
     "prop": {"killer.height": "tall"}},
    {"id": "A10", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Crane log: a lift every two or three minutes, 23:00-00:30, operator S.H. In pencil on the 23:40 line: \"splash 23:41 W side?\"",
     "at": [["P_Holt", "CraneCab", "23:00", "00:30"]]},
    {"id": "A11", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Gate book: \"23:25 Capt. Kordes in, harbour master. 23:55 out.\"",
     "at": [["P_Kordes", "HarbourMasterOffice", "23:25", "23:55"]]},
    {"id": "A12", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Slate behind the bar: \"No credit.\" Under it, never rubbed out: \"E.M. $40\".",
     "prop": {"morrow.debt": "owed"}},
    {"id": "A13", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Cash register tape: six rings between 23:30 and 23:50, clerk N.",
     "at": [["P_Nora", "Bar", "23:30", "23:50"]]},
    {"id": "A14", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Gangway watch book: \"Master ashore 23:20. Aboard 00:05.\"",
     "at": [["P_Kordes", "Ashore", "23:20", "00:05"]]},
    {"id": "A15", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Two crates stencilled MACHINE PARTS under a tarp in the master's cabin: cigarettes and Scotch.",
     "motive_of": "P_Kordes"},
    {"id": "A16", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Manifest copy: cleared by customs officer L. Varga.", "motive_of": "P_Varga"},
    {"id": "A17", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Envelope with $500 in fifties, \"J.K.\" on the flap.", "motive_of": "P_Varga"},
    {"id": "A18", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Duty roster: Morrow and Varga on CL-2, 22:00-02:00."},
    {"id": "A19", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Morrow's draft report on the Agatha: \"Hold search requested by telephone, 20:10.\" Unsent.", "motive_of": "P_Kordes"},
    {"id": "A20", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Harbour movements board, chalk: \"CL-2 out 16:20, in 16:45, hook lost P5. On station 22:00. Out 23:53. In 00:20.\"",
     "at": [["E_CL2", "CustomsBerth", "22:00", "23:52"], ["E_CL2", "OuterHarbour", "23:53", "00:20"],
            ["E_Boathook", "UnderPier", "16:45", "02:00"]]},
    {"id": "A21", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Agatha tally sheet, tallyman P. Doyle: hoists 23:00 to 00:30, crane S.H. on every line. Foot of the sheet: slung 140, landed 136.",
     "at": [["P_Holt", "CraneCab", "23:00", "00:30"]], "prop": {"cargo.count": "short"}},
    {"id": "A22", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Port clearance for the Agatha: \"Master seen 23:30. Cleared 23:50. Hold search waived.\" Signed R. Ashby, countersigned J. Kordes; for customs, L. Varga.",
     "at": [["P_Kordes", "HarbourMasterOffice", "23:30", "23:50"], ["P_Varga", "HarbourMasterOffice", "23:30", "23:50"]]},
    {"id": "A23", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Varga on the lower landing in the small hours, a lantern and a pike pole, fishing under the pier."},
    {"id": "A24", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Fresh gouge in the lamp post, higher than a man's head. Ash splinters in it.",
     "prop": {"weapon.length": "long"}},
    {"id": "A25", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Kordes passes Varga an envelope at the foot of the gangway, in its shadow, after midnight.", "motive_of": "P_Varga"},
    {"id": "A26", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Customs store book: \"CL-2 boathook lost overboard at Pier 5, 16:30 Fri. L.V.\" Below: \"Clearance stamp out to the harbour master 23:28, L.V. Back 23:52.\"",
     "at": [["E_Boathook", "UnderPier", "16:30", "02:00"], ["P_Varga", "PortOffice", "23:28", "23:52"]]},
    {"id": "A27", "kind": "anchor", "text": "The detective in the back-bar mirror, between the gin and the rye. Six foot one in his hat."},
    {"id": "A28", "kind": "anchor", "object": true, "text": "Tripod by the darkroom door. Ash legs, brass feet. One leg sawn short, the cut still pale, its brass foot gone."},
    {"id": "A29", "kind": "anchor", "text": "Print from the Meridian job on the drying line: a man in a customs greatcoat at the door of room 9, a woman's gloved hand on his sleeve.",
     "motive_of": "P_Detective"},
    {"id": "A30", "kind": "anchor", "text": "In the desk drawer: a Hotel Meridian envelope, $300 in fifties, \"J.K.\" on the flap, dated Thursday.",
     "motive_of": "P_Detective"},
    {"id": "A31", "kind": "anchor", "text": "The first plate in tonight's box, exposed before the night began: almost black. Rain in a flash, the rail of a pier."},

    {"id": "D01", "kind": "detail", "from": "SH_Wound", "text": "Enlarged: ash splinters in the hair. A long wooden shaft, swung hard.",
     "prop": {"weapon.length": "long"}},
    {"id": "D02", "kind": "detail", "from": "SH_CraneLog", "text": "Enlarged, a pencil note up the margin: \"slewed short 23:00-23:50 - CL-2 under the swing.\"",
     "at": [["E_CL2", "CustomsBerth", "23:00", "23:50"]]},
    {"id": "D03", "kind": "detail", "from": "SH_Notebook", "text": "Enlarged, the smudge reads: \"Cleared by L. Varga.\"", "motive_of": "P_Varga"},
    {"id": "D04", "kind": "detail", "from": "SH_Boathook", "text": "Enlarged: under the tar on the grip, a stencil: \"C.L. 2\"."},
    {"id": "D05", "kind": "detail", "from": "SH_Frame1", "text": "Enlarged: the end lamp of Pier 5, dark. Below it a man's hand thrown up against the flash, a customs button on the cuff."},
    {"id": "D06", "kind": "detail", "from": "SH_Mirror", "text": "Enlarged: a dry salt line on the trouser cuffs, shin-high. The right glove torn across the palm, a fresh splinter cut under it."},

    {"id": "S01", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Brannock", "true": false, "false_kind": "mistake", "cost": 0,
     "text": "Customs man. Dockers fished him out at ten past one. Slipped and drowned, if you ask me.",
     "prop": {"death.cause": "slip"}},
    {"id": "S15", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Brannock", "true": true, "cost": 0, "requires": {"refuted": "S01"},
     "text": "Then it's murder. The van takes him at six."},
    {"id": "S02", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Nora", "true": true, "text": "Left at twenty past eleven, angry. Said he had someone to meet at the pier. Your car was in my yard tonight, by the way. I thought you'd come in for one.",
     "at": [["P_Morrow", "Bar", "22:10", "23:20"]]},
    {"id": "S03", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Nora", "true": true, "text": "Leo came in half past midnight, wet to the belt and shaking. Ordered a double. Rain doesn't come up from below, detective.",
     "at": [["P_Varga", "Bar", "00:30", "00:30"]]},
    {"id": "S17", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Nora", "true": false, "text": "Elias? Paid his tab like a gentleman.",
     "prop": {"morrow.debt": "paid"}},
    {"id": "S11", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Nora", "true": true, "requires": {"refuted": "S17"}, "text": "Forty dollars. Dead men don't pay, detective."},
    {"id": "S12", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Nora", "true": true, "requires": {"cards": ["A07"]}, "text": "Every bottle in this port is mine."},
    {"id": "S04", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Holt", "true": true, "text": "In the cab from eleven. The end lamp went dark about quarter past. The customs man walked out there at half past; nobody after him. I'd have had him in my floods.",
     "at": [["P_Holt", "CraneCab", "23:00", "00:30"]]},
    {"id": "S16", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Holt", "true": false, "text": "Every crate I sling lands on the quay. Count them.",
     "prop": {"cargo.count": "complete"}},
    {"id": "S05", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Holt", "true": true, "requires": {"refuted": "S16"}, "text": "So I lifted a few crates. Check my log."},
    {"id": "S06", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Kordes", "true": false, "opens": "G_Cabin", "text": "I was aboard all evening. Ask my crew.",
     "at": [["P_Kordes", "Agatha", "20:00", "01:00"]]},
    {"id": "S07", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Kordes", "true": true, "requires": {"refuted": "S06"},
     "text": "I was with the harbour master about my clearance. Come down to the cabin, I'll show you the paper.",
     "at": [["P_Kordes", "HarbourMasterOffice", "23:25", "23:55"]]},
    {"id": "S13", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Kordes", "true": true, "requires": {"cards": ["A15"]}, "text": "Machine parts. Cleared by your customs."},
    {"id": "S08", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Varga", "true": false, "opens": "G_Locker", "text": "From half past eleven I was out on CL-2 in the outer harbour. Alone.",
     "at": [["P_Varga", "OuterHarbour", "23:30", "23:55"], ["E_CL2", "OuterHarbour", "23:30", "23:55"]]},
    {"id": "S09", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Varga", "true": true, "requires": {"refuted": "S08"}, "text": "I want a lawyer."},
    {"id": "S14", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Varga", "true": true, "requires": {"cards": ["A16"]}, "text": "Hundreds of papers cross my desk."},
    {"id": "S18", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Varga", "true": true, "requires": {"cards": ["A23"]}, "text": "Lost a hook off the launch Friday. Customs makes you sign for every one."},
    {"id": "S19", "kind": "statement", "speaker": "P_Varga", "true": true, "requires": {"cards": ["S03"]}, "text": "Slipped making her fast when we came in. Ask the pontoon.",
     "at": [["P_Varga", "CustomsBerth", "00:25", "00:28"]]}
  ],
  "monologue": [
    {"id": "VO_Kordes", "when": {"who": "P_Kordes"},
     "text": "Kordes lied about where he was. Men lie about murder, sure. They lie about money a lot more often."},
    {"id": "VO_Holt", "when": {"who": "P_Holt"},
     "text": "Holt robs the Agatha a crate at a time and writes down every lift. A thief that tidy doesn't stop work to kill a man."},
    {"id": "VO_Nora", "when": {"who": "P_Nora"},
     "text": "Nora was owed forty dollars. On this waterfront that buys you a black eye. Not a body in the water."},
    {"id": "VO_Self", "when": {"who": "P_Detective"},
     "text": "The face on the wall looked tired, tall and short of an alibi. I'd have pinned him myself. I just had."},
    {"id": "VO_Weapon", "when": {"with_in": ["A07", "A08"]},
     "text": "Every docker in Harrowmark carries a hook. Whatever did this had a longer reach."},
    {"id": "VO_Boathook", "when": {"with_in": ["A06"]},
     "text": "A lost boathook is a customs form in triplicate. Somebody always writes down when."},
    {"id": "VO_VargaLie", "when": {"who": "P_Varga", "lie_open": "S08"},
     "text": "Varga says he was on the water by half past eleven. A boat leaves a harbour the way a man leaves a bar. Somebody always notices."},
    {"id": "VO_Thin", "when": {"empty_any": ["who", "with"]},
     "text": "A wall full of pins and nothing pinned down. The night had cost me a box of plates and most of a pack of cigarettes."},
    {"id": "VO_NoWhy", "when": {"filled": ["who", "with"], "empty": ["why"]},
     "text": "I had a man and I had the iron. What I didn't have was a reason. Nobody kills a customs man for what he is. They kill him for what he's about to sign."},
    {"id": "VO_WrongWhy", "when": {"filled": ["who", "why"], "why_wrong": true},
     "text": "I had a man on the wall with a reason pinned under him. It was somebody else's reason."},
    {"id": "VO_Varga", "when": {"who": "P_Varga"},
     "text": "Varga lied about the launch, and the lie bought him a locker full of money. A man who sells his signature has to be somewhere to sign."},
    {"id": "VO_Complete", "when": {},
     "text": "For once the pictures didn't argue with each other. That should have made me feel better than it did."}
  ],
